# PHASE 4 — METHOD BODY VALIDATION

This is a critical phase.

Implement complete Tiny and Fat method body parsing.

For each MethodDef:

1. Resolve MethodDef metadata.
2. Read RVA.
3. Validate the owning PE section.
4. Parse method header.
5. Determine code size.
6. Validate the complete IL byte range.
7. Parse local variable signature token.
8. Validate initialization flags.
9. Parse instruction boundaries.
10. Parse optional extra sections.
11. Validate final method-body boundaries.

Store the following for each method:

- Metadata token.
- Declaring type.
- Namespace.
- Method name.
- Method signature.
- Generic arity.
- RVA.
- File offset.
- Header format.
- Header size.
- Code size.
- Local signature token.
- Raw IL SHA256.
- Full method body SHA256.
- EH section information.
- Decoder results.
- Validation status.

Do not use method name alone as a unique identifier.

Do not use arbitrary text windows to calculate method hashes.

Hash the exact byte ranges established by the parser.

