# PHASE 10 — REPORTING AND VERIFICATION STANDARD

Use the following status definitions consistently.

VERIFIED:
All applicable validation gates passed and reproducible evidence exists.

PARTIALLY VERIFIED:
Some validation gates passed, but material limitations remain.

UNVERIFIED:
Required evidence or validation is unavailable or has not been executed.

FAILED:
A required validation failed.

CONFLICTING:
Relevant evidence sources disagree.

Do not promote a status without evidence.

